Package: gamRTMB
Type: Package
Title: Distributional Regression with 'mgcv' Smooths and 'RTMB'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Jan-Ole", family = "Fischer", 
          email = "jan-ole.fischer@mailbox.org",
          role = c("aut", "cre"),
          comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-1556-9053")))
Description: Fits GAMLSS-style distributional regression models in which
    smooth terms may enter every parameter of a distribution, not only the
    mean. Bases and penalties are constructed by 'mgcv' and reparameterised
    with 'mgcv::smooth2random' so that the penalized coefficients become iid
    Gaussian random effects; 'RTMB' then supplies automatic differentiation
    and the Laplace approximation, and 'RTMBdist' the log-densities, each in
    its own native parameterisation. Restricted maximum likelihood is the
    default, effective degrees of freedom per smooth agree with 'mgcv', and
    smoothing parameters can be shared between terms and between
    distributional parameters.
